<p>7.2 &times; 10<sup>&minus;9</sup> <em>M</em> = [Ag<sup>+</sup>], [Cl<sup>&minus;</sup>] = 0.025 <em>M</em></p>

<p>Check: \(\dfrac{7.2&times;10^{&minus;9}\:M}{0.025\:M}&times;100\%=2.9&times;10^{&minus;5}\%\), an insignificant change;</p>

<p>2.2 &times; 10<sup>&minus;5</sup> <em>M</em> = [Ca<sup>2+</sup>], [F<sup>&minus;</sup>] = 0.0013 <em>M</em></p>

<p>Check: \(\dfrac{2.25&times;10^{&minus;5}\:M}{0.00133\:M}&times;100\%=1.69\%\). This value is less than 5% and can be ignored.</p>

<p>0.2238 <em>M</em> = \(\ce{[SO4^2- ]}\); [Ag<sup>+</sup>] = 2.30 &times; 10<sup>&ndash;9</sup> <em>M</em></p>

<p>Check: \(\dfrac{1.15&times;10^{&minus;9}}{0.2238}&times;100\%=5.14&times;10^{&minus;7}\); the condition is satisfied.</p>

<p>[OH<sup>&ndash;</sup>] = 2.8 &times; 10<sup>&ndash;3</sup> <em>M</em>; 5.7 &times; 10<sup>&minus;12</sup> <em>M</em> = [Zn<sup>2+</sup>]</p>

<p>Check: \(\dfrac{5.7&times;10^{&minus;12}}{2.8&times;10^{&minus;3}}&times;100\%=2.0&times;10^{&minus;7}\%\); <em>x</em> is less than 5% of [OH<sup>&ndash;</sup>] and is, therefore, negligible.</p>

